      "v": "THE BROCHURE'S BENEFIT GRID EXTRACTED WITH A DEMONSTRABLE ROW-SHIFT DEFECT AND NO VALUE HAS BEEN TAKEN FROM IT. The proof is on the face of the extraction: the 'Additional Hospital Admission Benefit / Max Day' row emits the values '- $10,000 $10,000 $10,000 $10,000 $10,000 $10,000 $10,000', which are Accidental Death Benefit amounts appearing on a Max Day row where a day count belongs, and the Accidental Death row then repeats the same figures. Where the grid can be read at all it disagrees with the live portal schedule on the Surgery Benefit at four tiers and on Mental Health at several - the brochure's surgery figures appear shifted one column left of the portal's from the 300 tier upward. That pattern is consistent with the extraction defect rather than with a real benefit difference, but it cannot be resolved from extracted text.",
